# Generated from output-i386-Release-0x601 and a Debug -DNO_ROSSYM=TRUE build by sdk/tools/gen_baseaddress.py --max
# (dwarf builds: i386 Release, which always sets NO_ROSSYM in gcc.cmake, and Debug with NO_ROSSYM)
#
# Layout policy (i386, GCC): ntdll sits at 0x7c920000 and every system DLL is placed below it, top-down, in the order of
# gen_baseaddress.py's PRIORITIES; user32 stays at its reserved 0x77a20000. The generator keeps growth room above every module
# (a quarter of its size, at least 64 KB) and 4 MB above kernel32, which carries one locale resource per supported locale
# (sdk/tools/nlsgen, ~2.6 KB each): about 1500 further locales fit before kernel32 would reach ntdll_vista/ntdll.
# Overlaps are rejected at build time: the check_image_bases target (sdk/cmake/check_image_bases.cmake; part of "all" and of
# the bootcd/bootcdregtest/livecd images) reads the PE headers of every based DLL and fails when two
# [ImageBase, ImageBase+SizeOfImage) ranges intersect or when a DLL below ntdll ends less than 1 MB under it.
# Regenerate after large size changes:
#   python3 sdk/tools/gen_baseaddress.py --max <i386 Release build dir> <i386 Debug NO_ROSSYM build dir> > sdk/cmake/baseaddress_dwarf.cmake.new
# (pefile is optional; without it the table goes to stdout) and keep this comment.

